3034-251a-59f4-b113-773134be1def" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396656 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396656 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396656 1084 #uuid "b0a7e325-bb6e-50d6-8115-8a687cfd729f" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396657 1081 "I only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396657 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396657 1084 #uuid "b53f607f-c200-5ff6-8ced-e452dc4d4a4b" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396658 1081 "III only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396658 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396658 1084 #uuid "dc8d5f4e-4f95-5ba3-ba2b-62b542d4c351" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396659 1081 "II only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396659 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396659 1084 #uuid "0481ca8b-da90-5343-99ae-63643fac6ed9" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396660 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396661 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396660 1069 "q-341642" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396660 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396660 1071 "Which of the following functions are piecewise continuous on $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\sqrt{x+1},\\,g(x)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & ⌈x⌉\\text{ is even} \\\\ -1,\\, & ⌈x⌉\\text{ is odd},\\end{aligned}\\,h(x)=u(x-1)+u\\,(x-\\frac{5}{2})+u(x-4).\n$$\n\nNote that $u(x)$ is the unit step function, and $⌈x⌉$ is the ceiling function." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396660 1072 #uuid "4689ffaf-d7a6-5ea0-9161-3ec67ff19338" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396660 1074 "Suppose $I⊆R.$ A function $f:I\\to R$ is piecewise continuous on $I$ if it is piecewise continuous on every closed and bounded subinterval $[a,b]⊂I.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$ The function is continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The function $g(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$ The function has jump discontinuities at $x=0,1,2,…,$ and any closed interval $[a,b]⊂[0,\\infty )$ will contain finitely many discontinuities.\n\n![](images/d5/d5a497337426dad07096702a3e211f525a959add8cb1fbaaef05fccac26d634b.png)\n\n- The function $h(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty )$ since it is continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty )$ except at the points $x=1,$ $x=\\frac{5}{2},$ and $x=4,$ where the one-sided limits exist and are finite:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}h(x)=0,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}h(x)=1\n$$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 5/{2}^{-}}h(x)=1,\\,{lim}_{x\\to 5/{2}^{+}}h(x)=2\n$$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}h(x)=2,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}h(x)=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f,g,$ and $h.$\"" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396662 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396663 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396664 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396665 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396666 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396663 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396661 1080 #uuid "7aedcafb-9859-554f-b742-1fe94afe482b" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396662 1081 "$h$ only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396662 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396662 1084 #uuid "70a234cb-554b-545b-99a9-38ca1d4a7d30" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [175921863