n [-5,5)$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396693 1072 #uuid "8061fba9-94fb-59ab-bb67-c981e34d25e7" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396693 1074 "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $2$ and $y$-intercept $4,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/d3/d33314230419ec762bc4ad8603b2e6c3436461cd6b4b6fe4783d12a23d01b660.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (10,\\infty )$ and $x\\in [-5,5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396695 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396696 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396697 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396698 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396699 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396698 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396694 1080 #uuid "fb55a4d3-ef9d-5ba1-bc8d-64b5b8502eb6" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396695 1081 "I only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396695 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396695 1084 #uuid "2d49c863-bcca-5003-b60b-2402ac1bbc16" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396696 1081 "III only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396696 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396696 1084 #uuid "372a1527-fcb7-5e97-9214-ceab892980ce" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396697 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396697 1084 #uuid "89d11ef2-0ebb-56ef-85f5-eff24a1c20ef" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396698 1081 "I, II and III" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396698 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396698 1084 #uuid "6e8bd46d-8040-58fd-9418-5e14e16fd9fd" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396699 1081 "II only" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396699 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396699 1084 #uuid "3ecd9f23-0f52-529d-9d3d-4b581fbbb61a" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396700 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396701 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396700 1069 "q-75640" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396700 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396700 1071 "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396700 1072 #uuid "2a792333-1cd7-596e-9f36-ea2d3aa5343e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396700 1074 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]=4[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=4{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}-4{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 4{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 4{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396702 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396703 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396704 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396705 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396706 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1077 "selection" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396705 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396701 1080 #uuid "5c4ee9d3-9826-59fa-81e1-d30802c66a1e" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396702 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396702 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396702 1084 #uuid "af7cf2f2-a407-5089-94fd-71e651ca7964" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396703 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396703 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [17592186396703 1084 #uuid "4693ebba-1176-550d-b873-45ee14bc37e2" 13194139533469 17592186045585 true] [175921863